# Tasks: Production Hardening and Garbage Collection

**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/021-production-hardening-garbage-collection/`
**Prerequisites**: [plan.md](./plan.md), [spec.md](./spec.md), [research.md](./research.md), [data-model.md](./data-model.md), [contracts/](./contracts/), [quickstart.md](./quickstart.md)

**Tests**: Included — the spec explicitly requests test coverage for nearly every mechanism ("tests must verify safe failure," "add tests for...", "add a concurrency test with multiple worker identities," "add pagination tests"), so each story below writes tests first, using this repo's existing convention (`node:test` via `tsx --test`, one `*.test.ts` file per concern under `apps/worker/tests/queue/` or `apps/web/tests/<suite>/`).

**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story (P1 → P3, matching `spec.md`) so each story is independently implementable, testable, and deployable. Per the plan's steering note, this phase is framed as **existing-infrastructure → production-grade integration**: most tasks below explicitly say whether they wire up/extend/test something already built (`recovery-scanner.ts`, `import-timeout-scanner.ts`, `job-lock.ts`, `enqueue-job.ts`, `import-cleanup.ts`, `label-form.tsx`, `AssetNavigator`) versus write genuinely new code — do not re-implement anything marked "already correct."

