- [X] T011 [US1] Implement `failRunawayJobs` in the same module: anchored on `lockedAt` (the *current* owner's claim time, not `startedAt` which persists across retries) rather than a lease check, so it overrides an even-still-valid lease once a Job has run too long; same retry/dead-letter branch, `errorCode: MAX_RUNTIME_EXCEEDED`. (Used `errorCode`/`JOB_RECOVERED`/`JOB_DEAD_LETTERED` — the existing vocabulary — rather than the separately-named `JOB_STALE_TIMEOUT` kind from T006, since the outcome is identical in shape to lease-based recovery and duplicating the vocabulary added no signal; `JOB_STALE_TIMEOUT` remains reserved in the allowlist for a future use if one appears.)
