**Goal**: Per-user Redis-backed rate limiting on the job-creating routes rejects excess requests with a consistent `429`, never touches internal worker operations, and never blocks legitimate in-budget usage.

**Independent Test**: Submit requests up to the configured limit (all succeed), one more (rejected with `429`), wait for window rollover (succeeds again); a second user is unaffected. Per `quickstart.md` §US7.

