## Phase 10: User Story 8 - Large Lists Stay Fast and Usable as Data Grows (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Every previously-unbounded list endpoint returns a capped page; the Properties Panel's Assets tab shows 10 per page; its Labels tab gains full name/color/color-code creation; "Add defaults" is explained in place.

**Independent Test**: Seed 20+ datasets/labels and 15+ assets in one dataset; confirm bounded pagination envelopes, Properties Panel 10-per-page behavior, label-creation parity with `/labels`, and unchanged asset/JobEvent pagination. Per `quickstart.md` §US8.

**Pre-implementation audit** (explicit instruction: audit and reuse the existing request-dedup/caching mechanisms — `dataset-labels-store.ts` and `dedupeInFlight` in `ai-task-api-client.ts` — before adding any new one). Traced every one of the 5 in-scope endpoints to its actual internal consumer(s) before writing a line of implementation:
  - `GET /api/datasets` — **zero internal consumers.** `(app)/datasets/page.tsx` is a Server Component running its own direct `db.dataset.findMany` with its own cursor pagination; it never calls this route.
  - `GET /api/datasets/[datasetId]/labels` — sole consumer is `dataset-labels-store.ts`'s `ensureLoaded` (module-singleton Zustand store, already built). Reused as-is, untouched.
  - `GET /api/source-connections` — **zero internal consumers.** `imports-screen.tsx` (renders `ImportForm`) is a Server Component running its own direct `db.sourceConnection.findMany`; it never calls this route either — same pattern as `/api/datasets`.
  - `GET /api/ai/models` — sole consumer is `listActiveAiModelsClient()` in `ai-task-api-client.ts`, already coalesced through its own `dedupeInFlight`. Reused as-is, untouched; it reads only `payload.data.models` and ignores unknown fields.
  - `GET /api/assets/[assetId]/annotations` — consumer is `getAssetAnnotations` → `image-engine.tsx`'s `applyAiResults(taskId)`, which re-fetches **every** annotation on an asset and filters client-side for one AI task's results. **This is the one endpoint where true pagination would be a correctness regression** (would silently drop AI-detect results past the first page) — deviated from `research.md`'s original assumption and applied a defensive `take` ceiling instead of a page/pageSize/total envelope; documented below.
